    {
      "id": "p0220-b009",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The Japanese language includes three separate writing systems, which complicates the process of searching for keywords in the player’s essay. For example, the word bibō (“good looks”) can be written with a combination of all three systems, leading to multiple possible spellings:",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.290192,
          0.543571,
          0.898888,
          0.615714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29113609326671425,
          0.5454785714285714,
          0.9068838584684409,
          0.6176214285714285
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "日语包含三种书写系统，这使得在玩家文章中搜索关键词变得复杂。例如，bibō（“美貌”）可以用这三种书写系统组合写出，因而有多种可能的写法：",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 37,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2962081506406988,
          0.5464285714285714,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.61
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "background": "transparent",
        "font_weight": 450,
        "text_align": "justify"
      },
      "notes": "",
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2962081506406988,
          0.5464285714285714,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.61
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29
      },
      "annotations": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0220-b010",
      "kind": "list",
      "source": {
        "text": "びぼう (all hiragana)\nビボウ (all katakana)\n美貌 (all kanji)\n美ぼう (kanji + hiragana)\n美ボウ (kanji + katakana)\nび貌 (hiragana + kanji)\nビ貌 (katakana + kanji)",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.309403,
          0.625,
          0.879676,
          0.700714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.31142432276265253,
          0.62595,
          0.9058694469936439,
          0.6980928571428572
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "びぼう（全平假名）\nビボウ（全片假名）\n美貌（全汉字）\n美ぼう（汉字＋平假名）\n美ボウ（汉字＋片假名）\nび貌（平假名＋汉字）\nビ貌（片假名＋汉字）",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.317510791611434,
          0.625,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.7064285714285714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.4,
        "background": "transparent",
        "font_weight": 450,
        "column_gap": 52
      },
      "notes": "保留日文拼写；原位预览采用两栏列表。",
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.317510791611434,
          0.625,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.7064285714285714
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 28
      },
      "annotations": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0220-b011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "To simplify this technical problem, the localization team disabled kanji support. The team then added new programming that internally converts every katakana character to hiragana.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.290192,
          0.707857,
          0.898888,
          0.760714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29113609326671425,
          0.7088071428571429,
          0.9068838584684409,
          0.7614285714285715
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "为简化这一技术问题，本地化团队禁用了汉字支持，随后加入新程序，在内部把每个片假名字符转换成平假名。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2962081506406988,
          0.7157142857142857,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.7592857142857142
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "line_height": 1.45,
        "background": "transparent",
        "font_weight": 450,
        "text_align": "justify"
      },
      "notes": "",
      "calibration": {
        "bbox": [
          0.2962081506406988,
          0.7157142857142857,
          0.9018118010944562,
          0.7592857142857142
        ],
        "font_size": 20,
        "leading": 29
      },
      "annotations": []
    },
    {
      "id": "p0220-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "This technical solution simplified matters greatly, but it had an unexpected flaw: the game’s core programming already uses the “Z” and “X” keys for other in-game functions. To get around this, the localization team made sure that no Japanese keywords required the “Z” or “X” keys. The team then added an on-screen message stating that “Z” and “X” are unavailable. Fortunately, these keys aren’t 100% vital for Japanese input to begin with – there are often multiple ways to type a single word in Japanese.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.290192,
          0.771429,
          0.898888,
          0.899286
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.29113609326671425,
          0.7730928571428571,
          0.9068838584684409,
          0.9009499999999999
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "这项技术方案大大简化了问题，但也带来了一个意料之外的缺陷：游戏的核心程序已经把“Z”和“X”键用于其他游戏功能。为此，本地化团队确保所有日文关键词都不必用到“Z”或“X”键，并增加了提示，说明这两个键不可用。幸好，日文输入并非一定需要它们——同一个日语词往往有多种输入方式。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": []
      },
      "layout": {
